{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Also to punish the righteous is not good</b> — It is joined to the preceding verse both front and back, and also includes the bribe that a wicked man takes, and afterward the righteous man is punished. So too, to punish the righteous in his judgment — the punishing is not good, for there the verb functions as a verbal noun, and it is not good to strike the noble for their uprightness."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:24.910435385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}